   "text": "The 1950 effort: local-language material at scale, judged weak and badly aimed by its own officials",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "In early 1950 the Department was expanding information work in Southeast Asia while its own officials, back from a regional tour, judged the output weak and aimed at no one in particular. The 1953 and 1954 papers show the same programme as a psychological strategy built round a base country and as a thin, budget-cut inventory of centres, films and radio hours."
  },
  {
