   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "excerpt",
   "volumeId": "frus1952-54v12p2",
   "documentId": "d60",
   "text": "One of our most serious handicaps has been that we have necessarily been too conspicuous in Burma with too many Americans in evidence and too much involvement in what Burmese consider their own internal affairs."
  },
  {
   "kind": "excerpt",
   "volumeId": "frus1952-54v12p2",
   "documentId": "d60",
   "text": "Bulk of Burmese people simply unable understand aid in terms of altruism."
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
   "volumeId": "frus1952-54v13p2",
   "documentId": "d992",
   "notes": [
